Subject: server: refuse media embeddings when GPU offload is active

Media (image/audio) inputs on /v1/embeddings or /embedding crash the GPU
backend: an async fault in graph compute of the embd-input + pooled-
embeddings graph kills the process with a bare SIGSEGV (100% repro on
Metal, M4, -ngl 999, any pooling type; no GGML_ASSERT output). The same
requests succeed on the CPU backend, text embeddings work on GPU, and
chat with media works on GPU — only the media x embeddings x GPU combo
dies. Debugging notes in docs/mm-embedding.md; root cause is somewhere
in the async GPU execution of the embd-input graph and survives
GGML_METAL_CONCURRENCY_DISABLE / GGML_METAL_FUSION_DISABLE.

Until the root cause is fixed, refuse such requests with a clear error
(ERROR_TYPE_NOT_SUPPORTED) pointing at -ngl 0, instead of crashing the
server. The check requires an actual GPU device to be present, so
CPU-only machines running with the default -ngl 999 are unaffected.

--- a/tools/server/server-context.cpp
+++ b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
@@ -4749,6 +4749,21 @@
             res->error(format_error_response("Input content cannot be empty", ERROR_TYPE_INVALID_REQUEST));
             return res;
         }
+
+        // media (image/audio) inputs in pooled-embedding batches crash the GPU
+        // backend (async fault in graph compute of the embd-input + pooling
+        // graph; 100% repro on Metal). Refuse with a clear error instead of
+        // segfaulting. Text embeddings on GPU and media embeddings on CPU work.
+        if (tokens.has_media() && params.n_gpu_layers != 0 &&
+                ggml_backend_dev_by_type(GGML_BACKEND_DEVICE_TYPE_GPU) != nullptr) {
+            res->error(format_error_response(
+                "Media embeddings are not supported with GPU offload on this build "
+                "(GPU backend crash in the media + pooled-embeddings graph). "
+                "Restart the server with -ngl 0 (GEMMA4_NGL=0 make serve) to embed "
+                "images/audio on the CPU backend.",
+                ERROR_TYPE_NOT_SUPPORTED));
+            return res;
+        }
     }
 
     int embd_normalize = params.embd_normalize;
